==Trivia==
*Like [[Never Summer! (Monthly Event)|Never Summer!]], Never Not Summer's Japanese name, Datte Chō Natsu Janyāi!, is a reference to the 1993 hit single "[https://youtu.be/ZA86CE_te-M Datte Natsu Janai!]" by [[wikipedia:Tube (band)|Tube]].
*Also like Never Summer!, each Never Not Summer! stage's Japanese name is a reference to a different song:
**[[Leak Year|Stage 1]]: Shōben Jidai = "[https://youtu.be/uRHn8J8Ou7E Shōnen Jidai]" by [[wikipedia:Yosui Inoue|Yosui Inoue]]
**[[Cats of Yesterday|Stage 2]]: Neko no Hi no 1993 "[https://youtu.be/Kj57YmedrlI Natsu no Hi no 1993]" by [[wikipedia:ja:class (音楽グループ)|class]]
**[[Heat Wave Blues|Stage 3]]: Summertime Blues Three = "[https://youtu.be/L97GrvDPocc Summertime Blues]" by [[wikipedia:Misato Watanabe|Misato Watanabe]]
**[[Lazy Tomorrow|Stage 4]]: Natsu no Jō-san = "[https://youtu.be/TBzqcsaT3K0 Natsu no Ojō-san]" by [[wikipedia:Ikue Sakakibara|Ikue Sakakibara]]
**[[Young Nyan|Stage 5]]: YOUNG NYAN = "[https://youtu.be/aw_4hqLDsrI YOUNG MAN]" by [[wikipedia:Hideki Saijo|Hideki Saijo]]
***"Natsu no Ojō-san" is the only song referenced to come from the 1970s rather than the 90s.
***Stage 5 is still called Young Nyan in [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]], making it the only stage whose reference wasn't lost in translation.
***It is one of the three events to have such a naming scheme, the others being Never Summer! and [[Cats in the Snow]].

